    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS). The only remaining references to the old names are in the test itself, which deliberately asserts they're gone.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 the DTOs are code-generated from this at build time:\n- Replaced the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single read-only `memberId`.\n- Removed the `checkDigit` property.\n- Updated the `locality` description to reference the member id's region segment.\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`): renamed the `customerCode` field/`customer_code` column and its accessors to `memberId`/`member_id`.\n\n**DB schema** (all four dialects): renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to hold the longer id).\n\n**Mapper** (`OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Removed the `membershipNumber()` and `checkDigit()` derivations and their `@Mapping`s; `memberId` now auto-maps from the stored field.\n- Rewrote `locality()` to read the leading region out of the member id (falling back to postcode/city when absent), and `fiscalYear()` to read the FY segment out of the member id \u2014 so the owner segment (via locality) and the fiscal-year value both reference the member id. Added `memberIdRegion`/`memberIdFiscalYear` helpers.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Replaced `buildCustomerCode` with `buildMemberId`: `REGION` + 2-digit `FY` (from the business-day-adjusted registration date) + `HASH8` (same SHA-256 prefix over telephone+lastName) + Luhn `CHK` over the base digits, with collision de-duplication now applied to the full member id.\n- Added a `luhnCheckDigit` helper matching the standard/test algorithm.\n- Pointed `primaryIdentifier` at the member id and updated the audit log line + `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (`memberId`) so the audit record references the member id.\n\nVerified the produced id (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`) decodes correctly: `NSW` region, `27` (FY2027 for an Aug 2026 registration), the 8-hex hash, and a valid Luhn check digit `1`.",
